Updates pushed. Added the Redis lock with a 5-second TTL and refactored to use DI for the cache.

Ready for another look when you get a chance.

{author_name}

LGTM! Approved.

Nice solution on the locking. Go ahead and merge when CI passes.

{reviewer_name}

Looking at it now.

Infra looks healthy - CPU and memory normal across all pods. However, I'm seeing some unusual network latency to the Redis cluster. Checking if there's an AWS issue.

{devops_name}

Found it. The orders endpoint is timing out on cache reads. Looking at the Redis logs, we're hitting max connections.

This might be related to the batch job that runs at this time - it's been growing in size. {oncall_engineer_name}, can you temporarily pause the order-sync cronjob while I push a fix to increase the connection pool?

{backend_dev_name}

Cronjob paused. Error rate is already dropping - down to 2%.

{backend_dev_name}, let me know when the fix is ready and we can coordinate the deploy.

{oncall_engineer_name}

Fix deployed and verified in staging. {devops_name}, can you push to prod?

I've also added connection pool metrics to our dashboard so we can catch this earlier next time.

{backend_dev_name}

Checking now.

The daily executive summary went out at 6 AM - that would have used yesterday's features. The variance is probably within normal bounds but I'll flag it to the stakeholders just in case.

{analyst_name}

This looks solid. Once you incorporate the feedback and recirculate, I'll give final sign-off.

Make sure to add the experiment to our tracking sheet and coordinate with Engineering on the feature flag setup.

{ds_manager_name}

With 200k samples, normal assumption is fine for the means. I'd just use scipy.stats.sem() and plot ±1.96*SE.

Bootstrap would be overkill here unless you're looking at medians or percentiles.

{reviewer_name}

Perfect, that addresses my concerns. I'm approving from the technical side.

{ds_manager_name} - over to you for final sign-off.

{ds_lead_name}

Good question - yes, all offsite replicas are encrypted at rest using AES-256. The encryption keys are managed through our KMS with automatic rotation every 90 days.

I can add an appendix to the report with the encryption details if that would help for the audit documentation.

{backup_admin_name}

Perfect, thanks both!

I'll update the ticket and send confirmation to the hiring manager. {sysadmin_name}, just ping me when the database group and license are assigned so I can close this out.

{helpdesk_tech_name}

Thanks for the quick resolution! I'll update all tickets now and monitor for any new reports.

Really appreciate the explanation too - helps me answer user questions better.

{helpdesk_tech_name}

Perfect. Calendar invites going out now for:
- Helpdesk training: {meeting_day} at {meeting_time}
- Post-pilot sync: Day after pilot at {meeting_time}

{sysadmin_name}, let me know when the updated package is ready and I'll schedule the pilot deployment.

We're good to go!

{deployment_lead_name}

Great feedback, both!

